<section class="h-band h-desktop" aria-labelledby="desktop-title">
    <div class="wrap h-desktop-grid">
        <div>
            <p class="h-index"><span>05</span> Desktop app</p>
            <h2 id="desktop-title">The flying happens in the sim. S4 OPS runs beside it.</h2>
            <p class="h-sub">S4 OPS is a Windows app, not a website you fly from. This site is where your account and your airlines live.</p>
            <dl class="desk-facts">
                <div><dt>Windows desktop app</dt><dd>Installs on the PC that runs Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Signs in with your account</dt><dd>The same account as this site. Sign in once and it remembers you.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Watches the simulator</dt><dd>Reads the aircraft state while you fly and records each phase as it happens.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Works offline</dt><dd>Sign in once, then fly without a connection.</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p class="h-cta-inline"><a class="button secondary" href="/Download">Download for Windows</a></p>
        </div>
        <figure class="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-caption">
            <ol class="flow-list">
                <li class="flow-node"><span class="flow-kind mono">Simulator</span><strong>Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024</strong><span>Aircraft state: brake, speed, engines, on ground</span></li>
                <li class="flow-link" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mono">aircraft state</span></li>
                <li class="flow-node flow-app"><span class="flow-kind mono">Your PC</span><strong>S4 OPS for Windows</strong><span>Detects OUT, OFF, ON, IN · keeps your logbook</span></li>
                <li class="flow-link dashed" aria-hidden="true"><span class="mono">when online</span></li>
                <li class="flow-node"><span class="flow-kind mono">This site</span><strong>Your S4 OPS account</strong><span>Profile, airlines, schedule, fleet and crew</span></li>
            </ol>
            <figcaption id="flow-caption">How the pieces connect. The desktop app talks to the simulator on your PC, and to your account when there is a connection.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>
